<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hussain Tekri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hussain Tekri is a Muslim shrine at Jaora in the Ratlam district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built in the late 19th century by a Nawab of Jaora and dedicated to the memory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a>. It draws large numbers of pilgrims of all faiths, especially during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muharram">Muharram</a>, many seeking cures for illness and relief from spirit possession.</p></div>
